    "description": "Software Engineer, January 2014 – Present\n•\tPlan airfield navigational aid (NAVAID) maintenance and monitoring system allowing local and remote connections from air traffic controllers and maintenance personnel\n•\tResearch and train for possible technologies that could be used in the project, including C#, HTML, CSS, JavaScript, RESTful Web Services, and SQL\n•\tGive the customer the ability to decide between alternative user interfaces by creating a C# application using Windows Forms for comparison with other possible user interfaces\n•\tDesign and integrate an application within the system using C# which allows maintenance personnel to remotely access and configure headless airfield NAVAID monitoring applications\n•\tDevelop user interface prototype using Windows Forms and agile development to incorporate customer feedback during each iteration of development\n•\tDesign software back-end utilizing UML Diagrams\n•\tDevelop code utilizing Microsoft Framework Design Guidelines for .NET libraries\n\nElectronics Engineer, June 2012 – January 2014\n•\tDesigned an automatic test program set for a circuit card in an aircraft’s Flight Control Computer\n•\tTransformed a customer-provided test requirements document into an automated testing system comprised of a test stand, adapter, and testing software\n•\tDesigned automatic testing software using NI LabVIEW, Microsoft Excel, Teradyne Test Studio, Adobe FLASH, and various programs developed in-house\n•\tUtilized available test stand instruments such as an oscilloscope, multi-meters, digital test instruments, cross-point matrices, 1553 and RS-232 communicators, waveform generators, power supplies, and relays\n•\tPerformed simulated fault insertion testing to ensure the test program set would detect and troubleshoot faults correctly\n•\tSuccessfully demonstrated system functionality through an internal configuration audit",
